ector":true,"transaction_code":"S","transaction_type":"sell","shares":900.0,"price_per_share":155.37,"dollar_value":139833.0,"shares_after":17695.0}],"_trap_components":{"decline":{"score":0.1,"weight":0.25},"balance_sheet":{"score":0.0,"weight":0.2},"value_destruction":{"score":0.026,"weight":0.2},"derating":{"score":0.0,"weight":0.15},"market":{"score":0.0,"weight":0.1}},"data_summaries":{"sect":["Its 14% operating margin runs 7pp above the Technology median (7%), a real cost or pricing edge over peers.","It earns less of the sector's profit than its revenue share would suggest (0.61x).","Over five years it has been losing share of the sector profit pool (-1.1% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.03 across 530 companies in the universe; the top four hold 29% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 72% over the past year excluding the latest month, though it has pulled back 34% over the last three months.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 49% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 70% and a beta of 1.41, it amplifies market moves.","About $38.6M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 53% in the 2020 crash, 42% in the 2022 bear market and 97% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $76.65 (margin of safety -29%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 6%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $60.15 to $101 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks expensive against Technology peers: EV/EBITDA 25.3 vs 16.4 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 39% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 3.5% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.7% (vs the 8% bar).","The 3 covering analysts target $150 on average, 51% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 46% clears the cost of capital of 11.7% by 34pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.19).","It runs a 41% gross margin and converts 13% of revenue into free cash flow.","ROE of 12% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.3x equity multiplier).","It spends 13.0% of revenue on R&D and 2.5% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $304.4M.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 7.7, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 4.77).","Working capital ties up about 300 days of sales, a drag on cash generation."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -3.0% over 3 years, 12.1% over 5 years and 10.8% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 30%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 11.4% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 21%.","Capex runs only 0.6x depreciation (1.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 22, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.7%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (11 sales, net $2.6M sold).","It returns 4.0% a year to shareholders (4.0% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 1.5% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 1,465 employees, each generates about $573K of revenue, 1.5x the Technology median, and productivity has risen 7.1% a year.","That works out to $73K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.2M (2x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $14K per employee."]},"profile":